Emma squeezes her slender shoulders through a narrow, splintered vertical gap in the rotting hull of the sunken wooden ship, her hand sliding free from Noah's fingers. Viewed in an over-the-shoulder shot from behind Noah, the frame crops Noah's blonde hair and the sleeveless shoulder of his orange scaled mermaid top as he hovers outside the timber wall, his blue eyes watching Emma anxiously as his broad forked tail fin proves too wide to follow. Inside the gap, Emma turns to face the murky interior of the ship, her wavy brown ponytail swirling in the shadowed water, her brown eyes peering nervously into the darkness as her green mermaid tail slips forward between the barnacle-crusted planks. The algae-covered wooden hull rises several times her height above the pale sandy seabed.

---METADATA---
