A warm, shimmering beam of orange evening light pierces through a small circular hole in the rotting hull, casting a glowing spot across the curved interior wall. Framed from an over-the-shoulder perspective behind Emma, the shot crops the back of her head, her wavy brown ponytail, and the blue scaled shoulder of her mermaid top as she gazes ahead into the cabin. Deeper in the waterlogged chamber, Oskar the octopus jerks several long reddish-orange arms upward to swat at the dancing orange beam. His large yellow eyes with horizontal pupils glow bright with excitement, his bulbous mantle bobbing as his suction cups reach eagerly toward the shimmering light spot on the algae-covered timber planks.

