The palm-sized chunk of frosted blue sea-glass sits firmly wedged inside a circular gap in the dark, waterlogged hull planks of the sunken ship. A glowing, dancing dot of refracted blue light projects brightly across the curved timber wall, illuminating patches of slimy green algae and tiny clinging barnacles. Close-up shot focusing entirely on the thick, translucent blue glass lodged into the rotting wood, with no people present in the dark, quiet hull interior as faint bubbles drift slowly through the murky water.

